{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Then we will give, etc.</b> Here they employed great cleverness, for it is the way of the deceiver not to scrutinize the details of the conditions, and on the contrary, to seek to lighten the matter upon his counterpart so that he will agree to do the thing — for through this he will accomplish what he schemed to do. But the sons of Jacob inverted the matter: to uproot from the heart of their counterpart any suspicion of cunning, they said that the thing is a condition — <b>then we will give our daughters</b> etc., <b>and your daughters we will take</b> etc. — meaning that the authority is in our hands to give and to take, and this matter proclaims a clear sign that they speak with sincerity of heart, not with cunning in the world."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:54.901518629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}